WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.700
Knowing, understanding, mastery.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.067
People mix these three up, and that is why they study for a year and still freeze in interviews.

3
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.333
First rule: judge your level one topic at a time.

4
00:00:12.633 --> 00:00:16.767
You will sit at different levels for different things, and that is completely normal.

5
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:20.000
Here is the ladder, from the bottom up.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.183
Aware: you recognize the words.

7
00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:24.067
A glossary alone gets you here.

8
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:27.411
Practitioner: you have run the code and built a RAG.

9
00:00:27.411 --> 00:00:28.933
That is a hireable junior.

10
00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:33.604
Engineer: you ship with evals, latency budgets, and cost per query.

11
00:00:33.604 --> 00:00:36.800
This is the twenty five to thirty five lakh line.

12
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.633
Architect: you make correct tradeoffs, and can say we don't need AI for this.

13
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.971
Frontier: you create new knowledge.

14
00:00:43.971 --> 00:00:46.067
Studying alone never gets you there.

15
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:50.333
The biggest jump is between level one and level two.

16
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.620
A practitioner has run the code.

17
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.033
An engineer measures it, with evals and cost per query.

18
00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:58.523
A practitioner follows a tutorial.

19
00:00:58.523 --> 00:01:01.100
An engineer documents the failure modes.

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.800
The jump is measurement.

21
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.767
Pick any topic you have checked off, and run this test.

22
00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.400
Can you explain it to a smart non-expert in sixty seconds?

23
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.100
Can you rebuild its core in code without looking?

24
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.300
Can you name two situations where it is the wrong choice?

25
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.700
And can you show a number you measured yourself?

26
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.367
Say you have checked off RAG.

27
00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.533
Now run the four questions on it.

28
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:27.216
Most people who think they know a topic pass just one.

29
00:01:27.216 --> 00:01:29.533
Four yeses means level two or higher.

30
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:31.445
Let's recap.

31
00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:34.767
Knowing, understanding and mastery are different levels.

32
00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:37.133
Judge yourself per topic, honestly.

33
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:40.233
Level two starts when you have measurements of your own.

34
00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.747
And the four question test tells you where you stand.

35
00:01:43.747 --> 00:01:45.567
Next up: the canonical papers.
